{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017ro76xpH3fZJ9WmaTsvfqo","type":"tool_result","content":"   113→## Fix History\n   114→\n   115→### Attempt 1 Fixes Applied\n   116→1. **Cross-group epithet resolution** (consensus.py) - Did not produce expected results\n   117→2. **Article filtering for pronunciation** (cmu_proposer.py) - Partially worked (\"the\" removed)\n   118→\n   119→## Next Action\n   120→Run PROMPT_fix.md to address mention counting (Critical #1) - this is the root cause of both the character extraction and profile generation failures.\n   121→\n   122→## Key Insight for Fix Phase\n   123→The pronunciation guide shows:\n   124→- \"Prospero\": 18 occurrences\n   125→- \"Prince\": 9 occurrences\n   126→\n   127→But the character \"the Prince Prospero\" only shows 3 mentions.\n   128→\n   129→This proves the mention counting is NOT aggregating across aliases. The character extraction is finding the references (otherwise pronunciation couldn't count them), but the final character object is not getting the aggregated count.\n   130→\n   131→**Data flow to investigate:**\n   132→1. Where does `mention_count` get set on the Character object?\n   133→2. Is it before or after alias merging?\n   134→3. Are alias mention counts being summed into the primary character?\n   135→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a5027fd9-634a-4fbc-b2b1-f3c4543d4067","uuid":"c3136df9-9cea-48a1-91fc-1b5a3e146620","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/EVALUATION_STATE.md","content":"## Fix History\n\n### Attempt 1 Fixes Applied\n1. **Cross-group epithet resolution** (consensus.py) - Did not produce expected results\n2. **Article filtering for pronunciation** (cmu_proposer.py) - Partially worked (\"the\" removed)\n\n## Next Action\nRun PROMPT_fix.md to address mention counting (Critical #1) - this is the root cause of both the character extraction and profile generation failures.\n\n## Key Insight for Fix Phase\nThe pronunciation guide shows:\n- \"Prospero\": 18 occurrences\n- \"Prince\": 9 occurrences\n\nBut the character \"the Prince Prospero\" only shows 3 mentions.\n\nThis proves the mention counting is NOT aggregating across aliases. The character extraction is finding the references (otherwise pronunciation couldn't count them), but the final character object is not getting the aggregated count.\n\n**Data flow to investigate:**\n1. Where does `mention_count` get set on the Character object?\n2. Is it before or after alias merging?\n3. Are alias mention counts being summed into the primary character?\n","numLines":23,"startLine":113,"totalLines":135}}}
